# Preserve the exact document bytes used by contract digest fixtures on every OS.
# The vendored standards tree is verified byte-for-byte against standards-lock.json
# (sync-standards --check, hatch_build.py); a CRLF checkout would fail every digest.
* text=auto eol=lf
# The copier template and its byte-parity fixtures (WS2 R-2): the render
# is compared byte-for-byte against the fixture on EVERY OS, so both sides
# must check out LF. The global rule above already implies it; these rows
# pin it for the scaffold gates specifically, so a future relaxation of the
# global line reddens here instead of on a Windows CI lane.
template/** text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/scaffold_expected/** text eol=lf
# The phase-2 patch's two surfaces (issue #408): the patch is generated
# from the checked-out bytes and must apply to the checked-out bytes, so
# these must be LF on every OS — text SET (not auto) removes the
# auto-detection ambiguity the Windows runner's global autocrlf exploits.
great-docs.yml text eol=lf
website/** text eol=lf
